    "title": "Bill Murray attends Furman basketball vs UConn game in March Madness",
    "text": "FURMANWhy is Bill Murray at Furman vs UConn basketball game in 2026 March Madness? Zachary HuberHendersonville Times-NewsMarch 20, 2026Updated March 22, 2026, 7:32 p.m. ETBill Murray made the trip to Xfinity Mobile Arena in Philadelphia for the Furman basketball game against UConn in the first round of the Men's NCAA Tournament on March 20. He was spotted by the TBS camera crew early in the first half.Why is he at the March Madness game?The actor is a well-documented UConn fan.Why is Bill Murray at Furman vs. UConn?Murray has been one of the most prominent celebrity fans of the Huskies. His son, Luke Murray, is an assistant coach on UConn coach Dan Hurley's staff.Need a news break? Check out the all new PLAY hub with puzzles, games and more!Luke Murray joined the Huskies coaching staff in 2021 and has been to five consecutive NCAA tournaments and is a two-time national champion.Bill Murray was constantly shown during UConn's championship runs in 2023 and 2024.Billy Murray wasn't always a UConn fanMurray attended Regis University in Denver, a private Jesuit school. He grew up in Evanston, Illinois, and grew up a fan of the Fighting Illini.Zachary Huber is a high school sports reporter for the Hendersonville Times-News. Email him at zhuber@gannett.com or follow him on X @zacharyahuber.He Was Once An Icon In The NBA, Here's Him NowOutdoor Revival | AdAdUndo12 Things To Cut When Living On RetirementGreensprout | AdAdUndoNFL Stars Who Should Lose Their Hall Of Fame SpotExplored Planet | AdAdUndoBehind-The-Scenes Facts About The MunstersOutdoor Revival | AdAdUndoInvestors Scrambling Before Starlink Goes PublicProfitable News | AdAdLearn MoreUndoWhy Your Rotator Cuff Isn't Healing (It’s Not Just Age)Shoulder Relief News | AdAdUndo12 Things To Cut When Living On Retirement IncomeGreensprout | AdAdUndoMissouri: Say Hello To Cheap Car Insurance If You Live In These Zip CodesOTTO Insurance | AdAdClick HereUndoMeet Divorced Women In ST LOUISInstantalks | AdAdUndoTe